    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0290" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.001/48: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Port-of-Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-01T17:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. We understand that the French National Committee has issued instructions to
                    Bertaud to return to London with his wife by first available means. Please take
                    this matter up with General Patch<anchor n="61" xml:id="d255-f1"/> and local
                    British authorities with a view to facilitating departure as quickly as
                    possible. It is desired that their return to London be accomplished by means of
                    a route which does not involve transit through the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d255-f1" n="61" xml:id="d255-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Joseph D. Patch, Commanding Officer, Trinidad Sector and Base Commander,
                    Headquarters of Caribbean Defense Command.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
